# UI Rules

## Component Structure

```tsx
// 1. Imports (grouped)
import { useState, useCallback } from "react";
import { Button } from "@/components/ui";
import { useAuth } from "@/hooks/use-auth";
import type { UserProps } from "./types";

// 2. Types (if not in separate file)
interface Props {
  user: UserProps;
  onSave: (data: FormData) => void;
}

// 3. Component
export function UserProfile({ user, onSave }: Props) {
  // hooks first
  const [isEditing, setIsEditing] = useState(false);
  const { currentUser } = useAuth();

  // handlers
  const handleSave = useCallback(() => {
    // ...
  }, []);

  // early returns for loading/error states
  if (!user) return null;

  // render
  return <section aria-label="User profile">{/* ... */}</section>;
}
```

## Rules

- One component per file
- Props interface defined above component or in `types.ts`
- Use semantic HTML elements
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Use `aria-label` for non-text interactive elements
- Prefer CSS Modules or Tailwind — no inline styles for layout
- Test user interactions, not implementation details

## Responsive Design

- Mobile-first approach
- Use relative units (rem, em) not px for typography
- Test at breakpoints: 320px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px
